 - 原 D9 单变体只需记录两种对角斜率；融合后还要新增横向与纵向两个方向家族，否则无法识别红色十字与其交叉点。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/14/code.py:24:#     - 原题默认输出专用笔画互不相交；融合后第三步恰恰依赖交叉，因此 generator 要主动构造至少一个非触发交叉点。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/14/code.py:32:#     - 每个样例都强制存在主线中心交叉点，且该点不是输入触发器；这使第三步可被看成“所有交叉都变黄”，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/14/code.py:39:#       且至少一个非触发交叉点。generate_input() 通过“相交双主线 + 双真实触发器 + 预留所有笔画格”来保证这些前提。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/30/code.py:62:#    of corner thirds instead. The generator rejects legends where either signal would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/13/code.py:44:        - reflect the payload by 180 degrees around the midpoint of the line segment\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b0280bc/10/code.py:42:    Recolor the shortest path using the corner legend's ordered edge palette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/3/code.py:86:    \"\"\"Return the CCW quarter-turn count implied by a corner under a cyclic legend offset.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/3/code.py:242:    - The puzzle is no longer solved by raw bbox matching: the visible corner tag first changes each sprite's orientation, so matching sizes only works after applying the fixed corner-to-rotation legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/3/code.py:246:    assert out is not None, \"no valid fill under the canonical corner legend\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/39/code.py:199:    raise AssertionError(\"could not find the corner legend in any 90-degree orientation\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/39/code.py:218:    - A compact orange-framed corner legend contains a green L example with a yellow forward cell, plus blue-to-yellow count rows that define the bar radii.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/39/code.py:222:    - First rotate mentally until the corner legend is upright, then read the yellow forward step attached to the legend's L example and apply that meaning to the real L-marker's elbow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/39/code.py:226:    Key insight: The green L alone is not enough, because its elbow has two empty exits; the corner legend tells you which exit is forward and also upgrades every obstacle's radius from \"blue count\" to \"legend yellow count\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/39/code.py:386:    \"\"\"Paint the canonical corner legend.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/13/code.py:31:#      1. A corner legend is a small vertical 2-column table. Each row is a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/13/code.py:63:#      corner legend before building sprite candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/13/code.py:74:#      from touching grid corners/edges, so the legend is structurally unique.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/13/code.py:79:#    - Humans can read the corner table as a literal palette legend because its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/13/code.py:94:#      by the corner legend and reinforced by repeated source/target reuse.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/13/code.py:101:#       grid corner; that component is the legend and has width 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/13/code.py:305:    Fill the template strip by recoloring scattered sprites through a corner legend and matching them to guide-marked holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/13/code.py:309:    - Outside the strip are full rectangular sprites plus one small corner legend whose rows show source-color -> target-color pairs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/13/code.py:314:    - Read the corner legend to build a global color remapping for the outside sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/20/code.py:33:#      strip the marker, then decode the corner-to-rotation legend, then rotate the core, then\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/20/code.py:39:#    - Only four marker states exist (the four outer corners), and they form a cyclic legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/20/code.py:65:#      so humans can compare input sprites against filled output holes and infer the corner legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/20/code.py:294:    - The puzzle only resolves if the same global corner-to-rotation legend is applied to every sprite: after that decoding step, the rotated core masks line up one-to-one with the irregular hole masks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:109:def _try_extract_corner_legend(rot: np.ndarray, corner: str) -> tuple[dict[int, int], np.ndarray] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:158:    \"\"\"Find the corner legend under some rotation and return marker->radius plus its mask in original coords.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:163:            parsed = _try_extract_corner_legend(rot, corner)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:169:    assert len(matches) == 1, \"grid must contain exactly one valid corner legend\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:175:    Route the green path across the grid while each red obstacle bar reads its keep-out distance from a corner legend rather than from counting markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:180:    - One corner contains a 4-row legend: each row shows a marker color, a grey separator, and 1-4 maroon tally cells that explicitly define that color's distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:187:    Key insight: the bar markers no longer encode distance by how many times they appear, and the color meanings are not globally fixed; the corner legend must be read first, then applied to every bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/23/code.py:366:    \"\"\"Paint the 4-row corner legend on the top-left (0) or top-right (1).\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/30/code.py:52:#      line segment, even when inner bars float away from the global walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/39/code.py:57:     corner and not covering the legend's source or target cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/14/code.py:388:    - bg = azure (8). Red/blue obstacle bars (colors 2/1) are 1-cell-thick line segments perpendicular to the travel direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/29/code.py:231:    - The top-left corner contains a fixed legend rectangle made of two aligned 2x2 panels:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/9/code.py:35:#       every stencil occupies all four bbox corners and the legend anchor is chosen from a non-corner cell, preventing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/9/code.py:192:      its global quadrant selects which stencil corner becomes the placement reference instead of the legend anchor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/25/code.py:25:      1. Decode a 2x2 corner legend. It no longer means a fixed global offset; it tells which motif reference point\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/25/code.py:39:    - The same cue color is reused for both the corner legend and all block markers, which visually groups\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/25/code.py:67:    - Instructional pixels stay in two clean places only: one 2x2 corner legend and one singleton marker inside each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/25/code.py:72:    - Exactly one corner 2x2 patch encodes a legend mask from the three known codes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/25/code.py:117:    raise AssertionError(\"missing corner legend\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/25/code.py:279:    Recolor color-matched motifs onto marked 5x5 blocks, with a corner legend choosing which motif point anchors to each block marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/25/code.py:288:    - Decode the corner legend first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/25/code.py:670:    \"\"\"Reject placements where either large region touches any corner legend patch.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/25/code.py:674:    corner_boxes = [_legend_bbox(H, W, corner) for corner in LEGEND_CORNERS]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/25/code.py:699:    \"\"\"Render the sampled destination blocks, motif slots, and corner legend into the input grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/2/code.py:59:#    - The lookup legend is isolated in the top-left corner, while sprite templates and recolor legends stay\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/10/code.py:14:     each block now contains one cue-colored marker pixel, and one corner 2x2 legend says how that marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/10/code.py:41:   - The corner legend occupies one 2x2 corner patch, and generator rejects placements where the destination\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/10/code.py:42:     region or motif region touches any corner legend patch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/10/code.py:63:   - Exactly one corner 2x2 patch contains the legend mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/10/code.py:123:    \"\"\"Read the 2x2 corner legend and return the marker-interpretation mode it encodes.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/10/code.py:132:    raise AssertionError(\"missing or invalid corner legend\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/10/code.py:280:    Carve color-matched motifs into marked 5x5 blocks, with a corner legend deciding how each marker is read.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/10/code.py:289:    - Decode the corner legend first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/10/code.py:294:    - The cue pixel inside a block is only half the instruction: it gives a location, while the corner legend tells you which motif point should be attached to that location.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/10/code.py:674:    \"\"\"Inclusive bbox occupied by the corner legend.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/10/code.py:688:    \"\"\"Reject placements where either major region spills into a corner legend patch.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/10/code.py:693:        corner_box = _legend_bbox(H, W, corner)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/10/code.py:716:    \"\"\"Render destination blocks, motif slots, and the corner legend into the input grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/3/code.py:153:    - Every usable legend is anchored on a non-corner border cell: left/right edge legends define rows, top/bottom edge legends define columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/15/code.py:69:#     that legend corner with padding, so frame and legend never overlap or touch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/15/code.py:196:    - The bottom-right corner of the whole canvas contains a fixed 5x5 legend panel with four colored 2x2 blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/15/code.py:207:    comes from a corner legend whose own opposite-corner placement flips how its internal quadrants map\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/25/code.py:104:#    - The legend is restricted to a top corner band while real markers start several rows lower, so legend\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/16/code.py:156:    - Each nested glyph is anchored by its top-left corner at the marker position, clipped by the grid border, and legend samples with their labels disappear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/9/code.py:24:#      now contain a propagation-colored lower-right corner; we must mask the whole 4x4 legend patch plus its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/13/code.py:214:    - Paint the glyph with its top-left corner at the marker position, clip anything beyond the grid edge, and remove any visible legend sample plus its label marker from the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/34/code.py:110:    raise AssertionError(\"missing corner alignment legend\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/34/code.py:236:    - Decode the corner legend to get the shared alignment, and match each motif to the block whose color it contains.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/34/code.py:555:    \"\"\"Inclusive bbox occupied by a corner legend.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/34/code.py:569:    \"\"\"Reject placements where either large region overlaps any 2x2 corner legend slot.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/34/code.py:575:        for corner_box in (_legend_bbox(H, W, corner) for corner in LEGEND_CORNERS)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/34/code.py:595:    \"\"\"Render destination blocks, bicolored motifs, and the corner legend into one input grid.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/34/code.py:620:    legend_corner = legend_corner or random.choice(LEGEND_CORNERS)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/34/code.py:676:        grid = _gen_attempt(alignment=alignment, legend_corner=legend_corner)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/7/code.py:23:#      2. A top-left corner legend contains 1x2 pairs [A, B] on even rows, meaning:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/7/code.py:98:def _read_corner_legend(grid: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> tuple[dict[int, int], set[tuple[int, int]]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/7/code.py:121:    Apply two-color motifs to solid blocks using a corner legend, then pack the transformed blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/7/code.py:140:      corner legend; the other motif color stays as a visible accent inside the packed block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/58f5dbd5/7/code.py:145:    legend_map, _legend_cells = _read_corner_legend(g, bg)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dfadab01/1/code.py:74:#      corner was also (r, c). A legend, when present, was a pre-drawn 4x4 glyph with a same-type\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/14/code.py:37:#         corner cells become orange(7). The same legend therefore teaches both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/23/code.py:85:  - Split-line fg pixels are added as short connected line segments so the sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/40/code.py:28:#      one colored key pixel, and the four grid corners show four different legend colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/40/code.py:29:#      A kept component slides to the corner whose legend color matches its key color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/40/code.py:37:#   exactly four corner legend colors and exactly four central components are used. This is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/40/code.py:45:#   * control color is no longer \"the only non-bg border color\"; corners now hold legend colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/40/code.py:51:#   corner legend = four 1x1 markers at the exact corners; control pixels stay on non-corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/40/code.py:54:#   corner placements cannot collide. The central scene stays readable because legend, control,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/40/code.py:269:    color_to_corner = {color: name for name, color in scene[\"legend\"].items()}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/40/code.py:381:    color_to_corner = {color: name for name, color in scene[\"legend\"].items()}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/40/code.py:432:    corner_legend = dict(zip(CORNER_NAMES, legend_colors))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/40/code.py:440:        inp[r, c] = corner_legend[name]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/40/code.py:454:        tag_color = corner_legend[quadrant_to_target[quadrant]]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/16/code.py:26:  2. 唯一不接壤控制边的象限不再消失, 而是移到 split 交叉点附近的中心区域。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/10/code.py:65:#       * at least one ctrl-colored split marker line segment\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/13/code.py:47:#      pieces to touch one contiguous split-line segment. Every placement is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/35/code.py:22:        * 左/右区去对应交叉点的内角;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4a21e3da/28/code.py:95:  - Rays stay on their split row/column, corner pieces stay in corners, and the legend\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/64efde09/12/code.py:18:#    - 若把两个 sprite 做成互相垂直, 3 条水平射线和 3 条竖直射线会产生大量交叉点, 很容易\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
